---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Polaroid from '../components/Polaroid.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Alex Ainsworth: consumer product leader at Slingshot AI, previously Head of Product at Runna and first PM at Cleo AI. Also a former scuba instructor.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Hello, I'm Alex.</h1>
      <p class="note intro-note">product person, ex scuba instructor, part-time Dungeon Master</p>
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="lede">
          I build consumer subscription apps, mostly ones with some AI under the hood and some good for the world on top. I've been the first PM at a fintech, run product at a running app through an acquisition, and now I'm working on an AI for mental health.
        </p>
        <p>
          The part I love is building for people who can't tell you what they want. That usually means a lot of time in the behavioural data until a pattern shows up, then shipping something and watching thousands of people get excited about it. I'm happiest close to the customer and moving fast, and I will argue about onboarding flows at dinner parties if you let me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The logbook</h2>
      <div class="stack logbook">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="when">2026 to now</span>
          <h3>Slingshot AI</h3>
          <p>Product Lead on Ash, the first AI designed for mental health, at the a16z-backed lab building it. I look after the consumer product end to end: how people find Ash, start using it, stick with it and decide it's worth paying for.</p>
          <span class="stamp blue">NOW</span>
        </article>
        <article class="card tilt-r">
          <span class="when">2024 to 2026</span>
          <h3>Runna</h3>
          <p>Joined as the second PM and finished as Head of Product, as we grew from around 100k subscribers to over a million. Launched Runna's first LLM feature, grew one team into eight, and turned a long slide in beginner retention back into growth.</p>
          <span class="stamp">ACQUIRED BY STRAVA</span>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="when">2023 to 2024</span>
          <h3>Thirdfort</h3>
          <p>Senior PM for the consumer apps. Rebuilt the journey behind most of the company's revenue and led a scheme for sharing ID checks across the property market.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card tilt-l">
          <span class="when">2022 to 2023</span>
          <h3>Utila, Honduras</h3>
          <p>Eighteen months travelling, a year of it teaching scuba diving. More on that below.</p>
          <span class="stamp blue">SABBATICAL</span>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="when">2019 to 2022</span>
          <h3>Cleo AI</h3>
          <p>The first PM. Built the React Native app and the subscription product behind what's now a $400m+ ARR business, then became Chief of Staff for Product ahead of the Series C.</p>
          <span class="stamp">FIRST PM</span>
        </article>
        <article class="card tilt-r">
          <span class="when">2018 to 2019</span>
          <h3>Theodo</h3>
          <p>PM and agile coach, shipping products for everyone from Series A startups to investment banks.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="note edu">before all that: Economics and Politics at Exeter, with a year at IBM in the middle</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap underwater">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>The year I spent underwater</h2>
        <p>
          After Cleo AI's Series C, I did the sensible thing and took eighteen months off to travel. A year of it was spent on Utila, a small island off Honduras, teaching scuba diving: hundreds of students certified, from nervous first-timers to professional divemasters, and a lot of mornings spent on ocean clean-ups.
        </p>
        <p>
          It taught me more about product than I expected. Explaining something complicated, clearly, to someone who is slightly panicking is most of the job. So is staying calm when the kit breaks, the weather turns and a boat full of backpackers is looking at you for a plan.
        </p>
        <span class="stamp blue">MSDT</span>
      </div>
      <div class="underwater-photo">
        <Polaroid caption="Utila, about 18m down" tilt={-4} size="small" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Off the clock</h2>
      <div class="stickies">
        <div class="sticky" style="--r: -2deg">
          <h3>AI operating system</h3>
          <p>I run my working life on a personal system I built in Claude Code. Either very efficient or a very elaborate way to procrastinate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sticky" style="--r: 1.5deg">
          <h3>Dungeon Master</h3>
          <p>I run a Dungeons &amp; Dragons campaign. Excellent training for stakeholder management.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sticky" style="--r: -1deg">
          <h3>Chillies and hot sauce</h3>
          <p>I grow far too many chillies and turn them into hot sauce. Results vary. Mostly hot.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sticky" style="--r: 2deg">
          <h3>Tottenham Hotspur</h3>
          <p>A lifelong lesson in managing expectations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sticky" style="--r: -1.5deg">
          <h3>Travel</h3>
          <p>Somewhere a little unexpected, ideally. Favourites include Cuba, Japan, Ukraine and Northern Iraq.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem) 0 0;
  }

  .intro-note {
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem clamp(0rem, 10vw, 10rem);
    transform: rotate(-2.5deg);
  }

  .logbook {
    max-width: 48rem;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .edu {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }

  .underwater {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .underwater .card h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .underwater-photo {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .stickies {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .sticky {
    background: var(--highlight);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.4rem 1.6rem;
    transform: rotate(var(--r));
    box-shadow: 0 14px 20px -14px rgba(20, 33, 61, 0.5);
  }

  .sticky h3 {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .sticky p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .underwater {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .underwater-photo {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      padding-left: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
